<title>USA: TABLE- Triple P Q2 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>TABLE- Triple P Q2 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second quarter ended June 30</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr	   loss     NFL1.50   profit     NFL0.01</p>
<p> Net	   loss	36,087   profit	   242</p>
<p> Revs			67,293		   76,414</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  24,087		   23,593 Six months</p>
<p> Shr	   loss     NFL1.70   profit     NFL0.13</p>
<p> Net	   loss	40,956   profit	 2,958</p>
<p> Revs		     136,660		  160,116</p>
<p> Avg			 24,087		   23,463</p>
<p>(All data above in thousands of guilders except share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Excluding the results from discontinued opeartions, Triple P NV's net loss would have been $1.03 a share in the 1997 second quarter and it would have posted a $1.14 net loss a share for the first six months of 1997.</p>
<p>One U.S. dollar equaled 1.9630 Dutch guilders as of June 30.</p>
